      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "26 patients (27 lesions) who had severe calcified and diffuse lesions underwent Rotablator treatment, lesion characteristics were type B2, Type C of AHA/ACC classification. There were no patients who had type A1, type B1 lesions. Procedural success rate is 96%, coronary perforation occurred in one patient but not necessary for surgical treatment. Non Q myocardial infarction occurred only in one patient. Follow up Angioplasty were performed 1 and 3 months later after procedures. There were no restenosis after 1 month, but after 3 months, 56% of patients had restenosis."},
